From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexander Sack <asac@pantacor.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Feb 2021 12:14:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/15] fix bug in initcmd split that would cut the rightmost
 char for whitespaced tokened components that dont have a leading/trailing "
 (quote)

Signed-off-by: Fernando Luiz Cola <fernando.luiz@pantacor.com>
---
 src/lxc/lxccontainer.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/lxc/lxccontainer.c b/src/lxc/lxccontainer.c
index 02069cd..ab8ebe0 100644
--- a/src/lxc/lxccontainer.c
+++ b/src/lxc/lxccontainer.c
@@ -789,10 +789,11 @@ static char **split_init_cmd(const char *incmd)
 			continue;
 		} else if (tlen) {
 			tlen += strlen(p);
+			tlen++;
 			t = realloc(t, (tlen+1) * sizeof(char));
 			t = strcat(t, p);
 			if (p[strlen(p)-1] == '\"') {
-				t[tlen-1] = '\0';
+				t[tlen-2] = '\0';
 				push_arg(&argv, t, &nargs);
 				tlen = 0;
 				free(t);
